Package: aoclda
Type: Package
Title: R Interface for AOCL Data Analytics Library
Version: 6.0.0
Authors@R: c(person("Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.", "AMD", email = "toolchainsupport@amd.com", role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Experimental R interface for the AMD Optimizing CPU Libraries Data
 Analytics (AOCL-DA) library. This package is an early-stage implementation and
 is not yet part of the official AOCL-DA release; APIs may change without notice.
 Provides high-performance data analytics functions optimized
 for AMD processors, including basic statistics, clustering (k-means, DBSCAN),
 classification and regression (SVM, k-nearest neighbors, linear models,
 decision trees, decision forests), dimensionality reduction (PCA, Kernel PCA,
 t-SNE), cubic spline interpolation, nonlinear least squares, kernel functions,
 distance metrics, and utility functions. For license details see the LICENSE
 file. For support
 contact toolchainsupport@amd.com or refer to
 https://www.amd.com/en/developer/aocl/data-analytics.html.
Encoding: UTF-8
LazyData: true
SystemRequirements: C++17
LinkingTo: Rcpp (>= 1.1.2)
Imports: Rcpp (>= 1.1.2), R6
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), covr, knitr, rmarkdown, roxygen2
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
